L15905: @* \[32e] Font processing.  As \pdfTeX{} should also act as a back-end driver,
L15906: it needs to support virtual fonts too. Information about virtual fonts can be
L15907: found in the source of some \.{DVI}-related programs.
L15908: Whenever we want to write out a character in a font to PDF output, we
L15909: should check whether the used font is a new (has not been used yet),
L15910: virtual or real font. The array |pdf_font_type| holds a flag of each used
L15911: font. After initialization the flag of each font is set to |new_font_type|.
L15912: The first time a character of a font is written out, \pdfTeX{} looks for
L15913: the corresponding virtual font. If the corresponding virtual font exists, then
L15914: the font type is set to |virtual_font_type|; otherwise it will be set to
L15915: |real_font_type|. |subst_font_type| indicates fonts that have been substituted
L15916: during adjusting spacing. Such fonts are linked via the |pdf_font_elink| array.
L15917: @d new_font_type = 0 {new font (has not been used yet)}
L15918: @d virtual_font_type = 1 {virtual font}
L15919: @d real_font_type = 2 {real font}
