L1021@P26: Similar to the document info section is the document catalog, where possible keys are /URI,
L1022@P26: which specifies the base url of the document, and /PageMode, which determines how the PDF
L1023@P26: viewer displays the document on startup. The possibilities for the latter are given in this table:
L1024@P26: value meaning
L1025@P26: /UseNone neither outline nor thumbnails visible
L1026@P26: /UseOutlines outline visible
L1027@P26: /UseThumbs thumbnails visible
L1028@P26: /FullScreen full-screen mode
L1029@P26: The default /PageMode setting is /UseNone. In full-screen mode, there is no menu bar, window
L1030@P26: controls, nor any other window present.
L1031@P26-27: 27After the ⟨general text⟩ of the catalog, a construct openaction ⟨action spec⟩ can be given, where
L1032@P27: openaction is a pdfTEX keyword, and ⟨action spec⟩ specifies the action to be taken when opening
L1033@P27: the document. This ⟨action spec⟩ is the same as for internal links; see section 4.11.
L1034@P27: Several settings can be made in one \pdfcatalog call, for example:
L1035@P27: \pdfcatalog {
L1036@P27: /PageMode /FullScreen
L1037@P27: } openaction goto page 2 {/Fit}
