L1039@P27: \pdfcreationdate (expandable)
L1040@P27: Expands to the date string pdfTEX uses in the info dictionary of the document, e.g., for this
L1041@P27: file: D:20260216073304-08’00’. The primitive was introduced in pdfTEX 1.30.0.
L1042@P27: 4.2.7 \pdfnames
L1043@P27: \pdfnames ⟨general text⟩
L1044@P27: This primitive inserts the ⟨general text⟩ to the /Names array. The text must conform to the
L1045@P27: specifications as laid down in the PDF reference manual, or the document may be invalid.
L1046@P27: 4.2.8 \pdftrailer
L1047@P27: \pdftrailer ⟨general text⟩
L1048@P27: This command puts its argument text verbatim into the file trailer dictionary. Example:
L1049@P27: \pdftrailer{/mytrlrkey /mytrlrval}. The primitive was introduced in pdfTEX 1.11a.
L1050@P27: 4.2.9 \pdftrailerid
L1051@P27: \pdftrailerid ⟨general text⟩
L1052@P27: Use the ⟨general text⟩ to seed the /ID value in the trailer, instead of the default combination
L1053@P27: of the input file name and starting time. If the argument is empty, the /ID is omitted entirely.
L1054@P27: Example: \pdftrailerid{}. This can be useful in making reproducible PDFs. The primitive was
L1055@P27: introduced in pdfTEX 1.40.17.
L1056@P27: 4.2.10 \pdfuseptexunderscore
L1057@P27: \pdfuseptexunderscore (integer)
L1058@P27: If this parameter is zero, and \pdfmajorversion is < 2, use ‘/PTEX. as the prefix for the
L1059@P27: relevant /Info keys, as was done through 2024. If this parameter is > 0, or \pdfmajorversion is
